<item><title>Dragon Quest announces new collaboration with Google's Gemini for in-person event in Tokyo after DQX's controversial AI-powered companion</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/dragon-quest-tokyo-event-google-gemini</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 28 Jul 2026 15:43:11 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/dragon-quest-tokyo-event-google-gemini</guid><category>Nintendo Wii</category><category>PC</category><category>Google</category><category>Square Enix</category><category>Dragon Quest X: Awakening of the Five Walkers Online</category><category>Nintendo Wii U</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/DQX-Gemini-AI-event.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/DQX-Gemini-AI-event.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Back in March, <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/companies/square-enix">Square Enix</a> announced that <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/google-gemini-ai-to-power-chatbot-companion-in-dragon-quest-x-square-enix-says">it was teaming up with Google Gemini</a> for an AI-powered "Chatty Slimey" companion on <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/dragon-quest-x-awakening-of-the-five-walkers-online">Dragon Quest X</a>, a Japan-exclusive MMORPG. Following a divisive reaction, another Gemini-powered Dragon Quest announcement is here.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/dragon-quest-tokyo-event-google-gemini">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item>
